Licensing of the nodejs/ workload
=================================

Material derived from Node.js: the injection patches (bugs/*/injection.patch,
patches/), and the Node.js test names, code excerpts and commit messages quoted in
oracle.json, meta.json and RATIONALE.md, as well as the TLS object parameters
(distinguished names, serial numbers, validity dates, extensions, CRL entries)
that some reproducers reproduce from Node.js test fixtures when they generate
their keys and certificates at run time. It is derived from Node.js's source,
test suite and history (https://github.com/nodejs/node, release v26.13.0) and is
licensed under the Node.js license (MIT), below.
Copyright Node.js contributors. All rights reserved.
Portions Copyright Joyent, Inc. and other Node contributors. All rights reserved.
No code from Node.js's bundled dependencies (deps/: V8, libuv, OpenSSL, llhttp,
...) is included; the injections touch only lib/ and src/.

Everything else in this directory (the bin/ scripts, tool/, the README,
marauder.toml, bugs.csv, bugs.json, the reproducers written for this workload
(bugs/*/repro.js, bugs/*/repro.sh, bugs/*/repro.expected.json), and the labels and
verification records in meta.json, oracle.json and RATIONALE.md) is Copyright
Datadog, Inc. and licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (../LICENSE).

The following is the Node.js license at v26.13.0
(https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/v26.13.0/LICENSE, lines 1-50: the license of
Node.js itself and of the parts originating from joyent/node; the rest of that file
covers bundled dependencies, which are not part of this workload), verbatim:

